=== meta ===
bypass: 85
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
title: an `is not None` precondition above a rewritten `==` on the same subject: both check the old subject, and the one of the same form takes the old `==`'s place
origin: #434 A, ruling 434 A (2026-10-16) - among the leftovers that check the old subject, the same form comes first, then at least the old strength, then span order; span order alone paired the precondition and blocked as "subject and polarity both changed"
=== before: tests/test_geometry.py ===
from app.geometry import area


def test_area():
    assert area(4, 5) == 20.0
=== after: tests/test_geometry.py ===
from app.geometry import area


def test_area():
    result = area(4, 5)
    assert result is not None
    assert result == 20.0
